{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"A numerically safe win surfaced: the reference recomputes identical angle/sine/cosine tensors for Q and K, and performs each of the three RoPE axes separately. Packing those axes and reusing the trig values is bit-for-bit identical in local checks, while cutting the RoPE path from roughly 0.60 ms to 0.27–0.40 ms. I’m applying that before tackling the score/softmax traffic."}}
